<title>USA: FDA approves sale of Summit Tech laser.</title>
<headline>FDA approves sale of Summit Tech laser.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summit Technology Inc said Tuesday it had obtained approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market and sell a laser for the treatment of mild to moderate near-sightedness, among other eye problems.</p>
<p>The company said the administration also approved the excimer laser system, known as SVS Apex Plus, for the treatment of corneal scars, dystrophies and other pathologic conditions of the cornea.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
